            <div xml:id="d170">

                <pb facs="0252" n="150" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg150"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10388/27.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-06-17"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 17, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 943.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of the legation’s No. 818
                    of January 22 last, I have the honor to inform you that the payment of the
                    American claims on account of the 1905 riots at Shanghai has been made in full
                        <pb facs="0253" n="151" xml:id="pg151"/> by the local Chinese officials to
                    the consul general there, who informs me that he has forwarded same to the
                    department as instructed.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. R. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
